  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0. Its parents (#1144, #1139, #1123, #560, #551) are merged; main merged in (open runs #1109 via PR #1147, no-core burnout #540 via PR #1160), so the diff is #539's own.\n\nExpected merges: other open work on the same stack touches the same files additively - #538 (skim passes, on #1139) and the #1147 (open runs) integration into #1144's stack. This PR adds fields to `WireContourOp` / `WireContourDto` / `WireParams` / `WireJob` / `WireVerdict`, a new `motion::wire_edm::tabs` module and a second wire section in `posting_wire::stream`; conflicts there should be keep-both. `wire-iso.cps` is unchanged.\n\n## What changed\n\nWire EDM tabs (#290 D6), off by default, and the hold law that completes #534's slug law.\n\n- **Op parameters** (`operation::types::wire_edm`, `project::wire_edm_dto`): `tabs: { count, width, at[], cutoff_condition }` (absent = off) and `capture: bool` (absent = false). Every tab key is optional in the file, so a missing one loads and is refused by name at generation. An untabbed, uncaptured op writes no new key, so existing project files are byte-identical.\n- **Generator** (`motion::wire_edm::tabs`, new): the count, width, positions and cut-off condition are each refused by name if missing. Impossible layouts are refused too: a gap (width + kerf) that does not fit on one straight side (a width at or past the side, a tab on the facets of a round), overlapping tabs, a stretch between tabs the start hole cannot reach without the kerf entering the product, and a cut-off condition whose kerf offset differs from the main cut's. The main cut leaves the tabs: each run is entered by its own lead, cut both ways, and left back along its own kerf, so the wire is never rethreaded mid-program. The cut-off follows in the same path. The path returns to the threading point once per run and once per tab, and `cutoff_split` reads the cut-off's start from that.\n- **Verify** (`sim::verify::wire`): `WireJob.cutoff_from` / `capture`. For a tabbed cut, the main cut must free nothing (`TabsDoNotHold`), and the whole path must free the stated piece. An untabbed cut whose slug drops is refused (`Unsupported`) unless a capture is stated. `WireVerdict.held` / `captured` feed the report line (\"holds its slug by tabs through the main cut; the tab cut-off frees ...\" / \"... into the stated capture\").\n- **Post** (`posting_wire`): a tabbed cut streams two sections. The main cut ends at a program stop (M00, so the operator secures the slug), then \"<op> tab cut-off\" runs with its own `EdmCondition`. The post script is not changed.\n- **Stamp**: the tabs and the cut-off condition's wire and gap are digested only when tabs are on, so no existing stamp moves.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/539-wire-tabs.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/wire_tabs.rs` (new):\n  - `a_die_with_two_tabs_holds_its_slug_until_the_cut_off`: a die with two tabs. The main cut never crosses a gap, the cut-off crosses each gap once each way, the gate passes with the \"held by tabs\" line, and the program has the main condition, then an M00, then the cut-off condition. **New NC golden** `tests/golden/nc/wire-iso/wire_contour_die_tabs.nc` on the synthetic fixture, with an invented second condition `C120`.\n  - `an_unheld_slug_is_refused_and_a_capture_passes_it`: the same die with tabs off and no capture is refused by name (\"drops unsupported\"). With `capture` it passes.\n  - `missing_or_impossible_tab_parameters_are_refused_by_name`: 13 refusals, each by name.\n- `sim::verify::wire::hold_tests` (new): an unheld slug refused or captured; tabs hold, then the cut-off frees; a closing main cut reads \"the tabs do not hold it\".\n- `project::wire_edm_dto::tests::the_tab_keys_round_trip_and_are_absent_when_off`.\n- Existing goldens are byte-identical: `wire_contour_punch.nc`, `wire_contour_die.cl`, `wire_contour_punch.cl`. `wire_post` / `wire_verify` fixtures now state `capture: true`, and their line assertions take the new \" into the stated capture\" tail.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/534-wire-verify`: green on dc3a06f1 (sim, motion, app, ui suites; 0 failed, 13.6 min). By hand: app `wire_tabs`, `wire_post`, `wire_verify`, `wire_contour`, `golden_cl`, `edm_machine`, `edm_conditions`; motion `--lib wire_edm`; sim `--lib wire`. Clippy `-D warnings` on motion, sim, app and ui (all targets) is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Not run on a real EDM control (#290 D10). The codes and conditions are synthetic.\n- No UI fields for tabs or capture (the op page is #535's). They are reachable through the project file and the MCP parameter patch (DTO).\n- Tabs on arc moves: the wire path has none today. A cut-off condition with another kerf offset is refused, not stepped.\n\n**Merge with main (2026-11-13):** both sides kept in the wire types (tabs/capture/cutoff_from beside stock/clearance/burnout/skipped). The slug scan keeps main's open-run and core arms; the hold law's capture check skips a burnout. New: tabs on an open run or a burnout are refused by name (pinned in motion `open_tests::every_open_run_refusal_is_named`, `burnout::tests::a_missing_or_misplaced_start_hole_and_a_punch_are_refused_by_name`). Main's fixtures that free a slug (`wire_readers`, `posted_gates/wire.rs`) state `capture: true`. No law was loosened. Recorded in docs/decisions/539-wire-tabs.md.\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM: tabs (count, width, positions, cut-off condition - all stated, none defaulted) hold the slug through the main cut and a tab cut-off section frees it; an untabbed cut whose slug would drop is refused unless a capture is stated (#539)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #539\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
